<title>USA: American Standard cancels cash tender offer.</title>
<headline>American Standard cancels cash tender offer.</headline>
<dateline>PISCATAWAY, N.J. 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Standard Cos Inc said its subsidiary, American Standard Inc, has terminated its cash tender offer and consent solicitation for ASI's $150 million outstanding principal amount of 10-7/8 percent Senior Notes due 1999.</p>
<p>The company said the offer was terminated because all of the conditions were not satisfied. It did not specify which conditions were not met.</p>
<p>The notes that have been tendered in the offer will be returned to holders, it said.</p>
<p>(-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610)</p>
</text>
